# Mission Runner Lite

> Quick reference for PIR (Plan-Iterate-Resolve) workflow

## Core Rules

```
1. Read-Before-Decide     - ALWAYS read _planning/mission_plan.md first
2. One Task at a Time     - Execute single task per iteration
3. Update Immediately     - Mark [x] right after completion
4. Record All Failures    - Append errors to mission_notes.md
5. Ask When Unsure        - Confidence < 3? Ask user
```

## Quick Start

```bash
# Phase 0: Initialize
mkdir -p _planning
# Create mission_plan.md (tasks + criteria)
# Create mission_notes.md (empty)

# Each Iteration
1. Read mission_plan.md -> confirm next task
2. Confidence check (4 dimensions, 1-5 scale)
3. Execute one task
4. Validate (compile/lint/test)
5. If fail -> reflect -> fix or record
6. Update Progress Log

# Completion
<promise>Mission Accomplished</promise>
```

## Confidence Check

| Dimension | Question |
|-----------|----------|
| Understanding | Requirements clear? |
| Certainty | Approach unique? |
| Clarity | APIs identified? |
| Risk | Side effects controllable? |

- >= 4: Execute
- 3-4: Record concerns, execute
- < 3: Ask user

## Self-Reflection (On Failure)

```
1. Why failed? (root cause)
2. How to fix? (specific solution)
3. Similar pitfalls? (learn by analogy)

Strategy:
- Simple error -> fix immediately (max 2 retries)
- Medium error -> record, next iteration
- Complex error -> ask user
```

## File Structure

```
_planning/
├── mission_plan.md    # Tasks + progress
├── mission_notes.md   # Findings + failures
└── workflow_state.json # State (optional)
```

## State Machine (Advisory)

```
init -> read -> check -> execute -> validate -> checkpoint
                  |                     |
                  v (low)               v (fail)
               ask_user          self_reflection
```

Can deviate when needed - record reason to notes.

## Completion Criteria

Output `<promise>Mission Accomplished</promise>` when:
1. All tasks [x] marked
2. Validation passes
3. Constraints followed

If incomplete at max iterations: report remaining tasks, no promise.
